---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactBand from '../components/ContactBand.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---

<Base title="About" description="About Fabrício Kury, MD: physician, health-data scientist and founder of Fab Health Informatics, LLC.">
  <div class="wrap page-head about">
    <img class="headshot" src="/headshot.jpg" alt="Portrait of Fabrício Kury" width="160" height="160" />
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Fabrício Kury, MD</h1>
      <p class="lede">Physician and healthcare data scientist in New York, working through my company, {site.legalName}.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p>
        I trained as a physician in Brazil. After med school I went to the U.S. National Library of Medicine at NIH and
        spent 3.5 years as custodian of CMS Medicare claims for 87M+ patients, with 16+ years of follow-up and billions
        of rows. That work led to papers in the <em>Journal of Clinical Oncology</em> and at AMIA, and to the NLM
        Special Act or Service Award in 2017. I then did a postdoc at Columbia's Department of Biomedical Informatics,
        where I built the Chia corpus, published in <em>Scientific Data</em>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since then I've worked across health data. I was the first Chief Data Officer of a health-insurance startup.
        I was a clinical informatics lead at the Regeneron Genetics Center and the OMOP/OHDSI reference at Mount Sinai.
        I led value-based-care data science at Wellvana, and I now build data products at Sparx, a New York health-tech
        startup. The constant is Medicare claims and the OMOP Common Data Model, and translating between what the codes
        say and what happened to the patient.
      </p>
      <p>
        I take on selected contract work through Fab Health Informatics: CMS VRDC Data Use Agreements, Medicare
        studies, data-model mapping and reporting.
      </p>

      <h2>At a glance</h2>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li><strong>Education:</strong> M.D., Federal University of Rio de Janeiro (2014), with study abroad at Harvard Medical School and the NIH Clinical Center. Postdoctoral fellowships at NIH/NLM and Columbia.</li>
        <li><strong>Data:</strong> CMS VRDC (RIF, SAS and Databricks), CCLF, Medicare FFS/MA, Medicaid, OMOP CDM, FHIR.</li>
        <li><strong>Terminologies:</strong> ICD-9/10, SNOMED, CPT, HCPCS, LOINC, NDC, ATC, RxNorm.</li>
        <li><strong>Methods:</strong> electronic phenotyping, cohort discovery, regression, survival analysis, program evaluation and real-world evidence.</li>
        <li><strong>Tools:</strong> Python, R, SQL, SAS, dbt, Databricks, AWS, GCP.</li>
        <li><strong>Languages:</strong> English, Portuguese (native) and Spanish. Happy to work with teams in Brazil and Latin America.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactBand />
</Base>

<style>
  .about { display: grid; gap: 24px; align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 720px) { .about { grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; } }
  .headshot { width: 140px; height: 140px; border-radius: 50%; object-fit: cover; box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--accent); }
  .prose { max-width: 760px; }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: 1.6em; }
</style>
